                <pb facs="0183" n="1143" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1143"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 5.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr. Bragg</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-03-07"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 7,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to answer your
                    excellency’s note, dated yesterday, relative to the case of the American citizen
                    Henry Brudigam, informing you that I have to-day forwarded your note to the
                    governor of the State of Chihuahua, and have requested him to advise me as
                    speedily as possible touching the acts complained of.</p>
                <p>Reserving the satisfaction of communicating to your excellency as soon as
                    received the reply of the governor, I reiterate, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno. Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
